"1\n00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,229\nThe Learning Brain. Series 3: Generative AI\n\n2\n00:00:06,100 --> 00:00:07,391\nEpisode 5\n\n3\n00:00:07,471 --> 00:00:10,305\nA tutor built on learning science\n\n4\n00:00:13,105 --> 00:00:16,155\nIn Harvard's largest introductory physics course,\n\n5\n00:00:16,408 --> 00:00:19,812\none hundred and ninety four students took two lessons each.\n\n6\n00:00:20,232 --> 00:00:22,455\nOne week in an active learning class,\n\n7\n00:00:22,586 --> 00:00:25,202\nthe other week at home with an AI tutor,\n\n8\n00:00:25,383 --> 00:00:26,609\nand then they swapped.\n\n9\n00:00:27,050 --> 00:00:29,400\nThe class was not a weak comparison.\n\n10\n00:00:29,783 --> 00:00:32,519\nIt already used research based active learning.\n\n11\n00:00:32,689 --> 00:00:33,945\nOn the same tests,\n\n12\n00:00:34,198 --> 00:00:40,055\nmedian learning gains with the AI tutor were more than double those of the active learning class.\n\n13\n00:00:40,533 --> 00:00:45,354\nMedian scores rose from a baseline of two point seven five out of six,\n\n14\n00:00:45,557 --> 00:00:46,713\nto four and a half,\n\n15\n00:00:46,935 --> 00:00:48,344\nagainst three and a half.\n\n16\n00:00:48,514 --> 00:00:52,124\nAnd they took less time: a median of forty nine minutes,\n\n17\n00:00:52,144 --> 00:00:54,183\nagainst a sixty minute class.\n\n18\n00:00:54,353 --> 00:00:56,446\nThis was not an off the shelf chatbot.\n\n19\n00:00:56,920 --> 00:00:59,435\nThe tutor was built on learning science.\n\n20\n00:00:59,753 --> 00:01:01,546\nIt worked one step at a time,\n\n21\n00:01:01,613 --> 00:01:03,329\nmade students do the thinking,\n\n22\n00:01:03,551 --> 00:01:06,968\nmanaged cognitive load, gave immediate feedback,\n\n23\n00:01:07,098 --> 00:01:08,961\nand let them set their own pace.\n\n24\n00:01:09,401 --> 00:01:11,598\nIt had the correct solutions built in,\n\n25\n00:01:11,716 --> 00:01:13,003\nto keep it accurate.\n\n26\n00:01:13,173 --> 00:01:14,898\nSet beside the previous episode,\n\n27\n00:01:14,918 --> 00:01:16,181\nthe lesson is clear.\n\n28\n00:01:16,628 --> 00:01:18,815\nThe same technology can harm learning,\n\n29\n00:01:18,835 --> 00:01:19,766\nor double it.\n\n30\n00:01:20,173 --> 00:01:21,639\nDesign decides.\n\n31\n00:01:21,809 --> 00:01:22,613\nA caution.\n\n32\n00:01:23,039 --> 00:01:24,359\nThis was one course,\n\n33\n00:01:24,379 --> 00:01:26,652\ntwo topics, and short term tests,\n\n34\n00:01:26,745 --> 00:01:28,848\nwith highly motivated students.\n\n35\n00:01:29,250 --> 00:01:31,864\nThe comparison class was already strong,\n\n36\n00:01:31,961 --> 00:01:33,629\nwhich makes the gain notable,\n\n37\n00:01:33,742 --> 00:01:35,398\nbut not a general law.\n\n38\n00:01:35,568 --> 00:01:36,312\nFor teaching.\n\n39\n00:01:36,714 --> 00:01:39,345\nIf you build or choose an AI tutor,\n\n40\n00:01:39,458 --> 00:01:41,898\nrequire that it asks before it tells.\n\n41\n00:01:42,284 --> 00:01:44,765\nLoad it with your own correct solutions.\n\n42\n00:01:45,104 --> 00:01:47,391\nUse it for first exposure to content,\n\n43\n00:01:47,411 --> 00:01:50,986\nand spend class time on discussion and harder problems.\n\n44\n00:01:51,384 --> 00:01:54,503\nAnd tell students why the tutor holds back the answer,\n\n45\n00:01:54,672 --> 00:01:56,483\nso they do not route around it.\n\n46\n00:01:56,653 --> 00:01:59,498\nA tutor is not defined by what it knows.\n\n47\n00:01:59,796 --> 00:02:02,480\nIt is defined by what it makes the student do.\n\n"
